# Single-node deployment: automatic HTTPS + WebSocket reverse proxy.
#
# Caddy obtains and renews the certificate for {$RELAY_DOMAIN}. This is the
# recommended setup when you run exactly one relay node. For multiple nodes you
# need an edge that hashes the `serverId` query parameter (see nginx.conf /
# haproxy.cfg); Caddy's generic reverse_proxy does not provide that.
#
# `/metrics`, `/ready`, and `/version` are intentionally blocked from the public
# listener. Scrape the relay directly on the private Docker network if you need
# Prometheus metrics. Caddy OSS has no built-in per-IP rate limiting: put a
# CDN/WAF (or a custom Caddy module) in front if you need per-client limits.
#
# `serverId` is a bearer routing secret in the query string. Do not enable an
# access log that records query strings.

{$RELAY_DOMAIN} {
	encode zstd gzip

	# Keep operations surfaces off the public listener. /health remains public
	# for simple liveness checks; readiness is available on the relay network.
	@operations path /metrics /ready /version
	handle @operations {
		respond 404
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy relay:4000
	}
}
